# Job Hunter — Cline Rules

## Project Type
Web application — FastAPI backend + static HTML frontend. Automated job application pipeline.

## How to Run
```bash
cd backend
pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
```
Open http://localhost:8000 for the dashboard.

## Key Architecture
- `backend/main.py` — FastAPI app, API routes, APScheduler
- `backend/database.py` — SQLite (settings, jobs, applications)
- `backend/pipeline/` — scrape, contacts, customize, send modules
- `frontend/index.html` — Single-file dashboard (HTML + CSS + JS)

## Config Approach
ALL configuration is through the web dashboard (Settings tab) and stored in SQLite.
No config files to edit. No .env needed. No API keys in code.

## LLM Integration
- Uses OpenAI-compatible API (OpenRouter, OpenAI, etc.)
- Configured via Settings tab: api_base, api_key, model
- Called in `pipeline/customize.py`

## Contact Finding
- FREE, no API key needed
- Searches DuckDuckGo for hiring manager names
- Generates email permutations
- Verifies via SMTP (no email sent, just handshake)
- All in `pipeline/contacts.py`

## Frontend Rules
READ `FRONTEND-DESIGN.md` BEFORE writing any HTML/CSS. It has the exact color palette, type scale, component specs, and anti-slop rules. Linear-inspired dark dashboard. Inter font only. No gradients, no glassmorphism, no emoji, no decorative icons.

## When Modifying
- Keep pipeline modules independent — each can be tested alone
- All persistent data goes in SQLite via `database.py`
- Frontend is vanilla JS — no build step, no npm
- API returns JSON, frontend renders it

## Dependencies
- fastapi, uvicorn, apscheduler — web server + scheduling
- python-jobspy — job scraping
- requests — API calls + web search
- dnspython — MX record lookup for email verification
- markdown2, weasyprint — PDF generation (optional)
